================================================================================
PARITY NOTES (web components/a11y/RouteAnnouncer.tsx → native)
================================================================================
The four REAL behaviours of the web utility are reproduced verbatim (no fabricated states):
  1. first-render guard  — the landing route is recorded but NEVER announced (the OS/browser
     already speaks the page on load); RouteAnnouncerProjector skips changes[0].
  2. deferred title read — web DEFAULT_ANNOUNCE_DELAY_MS=100 pinned in RouteAnnouncerTiming
     (native titles resolve synchronously from the route table; the navigator emission is the
     settle boundary — documented divergence, not a shortcut).
  3. empty-title clear   — a navigation with an empty title wipes the region (web setMessage(''))
     and does NOT advance the rotation counter.
  4. zero-width rotation — counter%4 ZERO WIDTH SPACE suffix so two consecutive routes resolving
     to the SAME document.title (e.g. /charging/1 → /charging/2) are BOTH announced.
Sibling to AnnouncerRegion (0001) + VisuallyHidden (0003): identical visible-inspector +
presenter-voicing architecture; the surface wraps a polite live region exactly as the web source
renders <VisuallyHidden liveRegion priority="polite"> (role=status, aria-live=polite, aria-atomic=true).

